dies leaving RUNNING is deferred to #9.\n10. A second `[[bin]]` named `delegate` in `src/bin/delegate.rs`, sharing the library.\n\n--\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\nClarification on ruling 3: the heartbeat field is `lastHeartbeatAt`, reused from `PollResult`, not a new `heartbeatAt`.\n--\n=== ISSUE 9 ===\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Preflight rulings (owner, 2026-10-01)\n\n1. **BUSY:** a second read-write `run` or `resume` in a locked cwd prints `BUSY <holderJobId>` on stderr and exits 3.\n2. **Gate timeout:** the gate is killed if it runs past the job's tool-idle window (`--tool-idle-ms`, default 1800s). There is no new flag.\n3. **Lock:** `flock` on `$TMPDIR/delegate-locks/<hash of canonical cwd>.lock`, held by the supervisor. The file holds the job id.\n4. **Idle defaults:** model-idle 300s and tool-idle 1800s, carried over from the host profile.\n5. **Change-set:** always lists the commits made during the run, plus a concern if the tree is still dirty. The #6 probe showed a delegated Claude commits on its own branch.\n6. **MCP:** the old MCP `cursor_run` path does not take the file lock. That gap is accepted until #13 deletes MCP.\n7. **Dead supervisor** (deferred from #7): stale-heartbeat handling belongs here.\n--\n=== ISSUE 10 ===\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Preflight rulings (owner, 2026-10-01)\n\n1. **Output:** `resume` prints the new job id, like `run`.\n2. **Cancel on a terminal job:** a no-op. It prints the record and exits 0.\n3. **Resume errors:** `resume` on a RUNNING job, or on a record with no session id, exits 2 with the reason on stderr.\n4. **Chain links:** resuming A as B writes `supersededBy: B` into A's record and `resumedFrom: A` into B's. This keeps the reason MCP added the pointer (commit 8b21892): a watcher on a resumed NEEDS_CONTEXT record must be able to follow the chain instead of acting on the stale question.\n5. **Cancel:** SIGTERM to the supervisor's process group, then SIGKILL after 5s. If `cancel` had to SIGKILL, it writes CANCELLED itself.\n6. **Busy cwd:** a read-write resume into a locked cwd follows the #9 BUSY ruling (stderr `BUSY <holder>`, exit 3).\n--\n=== ISSUE 11 ===\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Preflight rulings (owner, 2026-10-01)\n\n1. **`delegate models`:** an aligned text table with id, label, backend and $in/$out per 1M tokens. The default is marked `*`. Rows sort by backend, then id.\n2. **`delegate doctor`:** human-readable text on stdout, one ok/warn/fail line per check. Missing or renamed models are warnings. It exits 0 when there are only warnings, and 1 on a hard failure (binary missing, or not logged in).\n3. **pi and claude models before #16/#17 land:** `run` exits 2 with `backend not implemented`, and `doctor` prints a skip line for each.\n4. **Model table:** `backend` replaces `family`. The ids are the 13 listed in #11 and spec story 45. Grok 4.7 is priced as Grok 4.6.\n--\n=== ISSUE 12 ===\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Preflight rulings: orchestrator ruling (owner asleep; reversible)\n\n1. **Slow-run negative control:** no test-only delay hook in production code. The lane records the negative control in the PR instead: it adds a local sleep before `run` prints its id, shows the test failing, then removes the sleep.\n2. **Supervisor memory:** sample `ps -o rss= -p <supervisorPid>` (the pid comes from the status record) while the fake agent holds RUNNING. The same command works on macOS and Linux, so the test needs no per-OS code.\n3. **Latency endpoint:** wall clock until the process exits. `run` and `resume` exit right after printing the id.\n4. **Cases timed:** `watch` on an already-terminal job, with no timeout path. `cancel` on a RUNNING job whose fake agent exits on SIGTERM. `doctor` against fakes that exit 0.\n5. **Budget constants:** about 3x the local measurement, with the measured baseline in a comment beside each. No retries: if CI is noisy, raise the margin.\n6. **Fake agents** wait on release files, never on sleeps (the lesson from #7).\n--\n=== ISSUE 13 ===\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Preflight rulings: orchestrator ruling (owner asleep; reversible)\n\n1. **Crate:** rename the crate to `delegate`. `delegate` is the only binary; `cursor-delegate-mcp` is removed.\n2. **Code to delete:** `src/index*`, `job_registry*`, `tool_schemas.rs`, `progress.rs`, `validate.rs` and the MCP e2e tests, plus anything else only they use. The supervisor must not depend on `JobRegistry`.\n3. **Environment variable:** `CURSOR_DELEGATE_HOST_PROFILE` is dropped outright, not aliased. Setup moves the file.\n4. **Setup:** build the release binary and copy it to `~/.local/bin/delegate`. Move `~/.config/cursor-delegate/<profile>` to `~/.config/delegate/` only if the destination is absent; otherwise print a note and leave both. If there is no old profile, do nothing.\n5. **Old status records:** leftover `cursor-delegate-jobs` records get no migration.\n6. **Old-name references:** allowed only in setup's migration code.\n7. **Plugin:** the plugin and marketplace ids become `delegate`, version 1.0.0, shipping the skill only.\n8. **Running setup on this machine** changes the owner's `~/.local/bin`, `~/.config` and installed plugin. That is deferred to the owner: the morning report carries the exact commands and the `~/.claude/settings.json` edits. CI covers the rest.\n--\n=== ISSUE 6 ===\n","localExecutionTimeMs":9042},"isBackground":false},"description":"Fetch GitHub issues 17, 4, 6-13 with comments"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"tool_518d1a4f-a72e-4924-9620-11bb097c16f","startedAtMs":"1790845569289","completedAtMs":"1790845579016"},"model_call_id":"5d97dc51-aeb0-476e-a6af-a8d07968be1e-0-5p7g","session_id":"42a2d878-df96-4e92-9fef-880dad80ff16","timestamp_ms":1790845579000}
