{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"tool_911a93aa-63df-4227-a3c1-2702837340a","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"cd /Users/user/work/delegate-fixtures && git fetch origin main 2>/dev/null; git show origin/main:src/cli.rs 2>/dev/null | head -80; echo '---FILES---'; git show origin/main:tests/cli_e2e.rs 2>/dev/null | head -50; gh issue view 17 --json body --jq .body","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"tool_911a93aa-63df-4227-a3c1-2702837340a","simpleCommands":["cd","git","git","head","echo","git","head","gh"],"hasInputRedirect":false,"hasOutputRedirect":true,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"cd","args":[{"type":"word","value":"/Users/user/work/delegate-fixtures"}],"fullText":"cd /Users/user/work/delegate-fixtures"},{"name":"git","args":[{"type":"word","value":"fetch"},{"type":"word","value":"origin"},{"type":"word","value":"main"}],"fullText":"git fetch origin main"},{"name":"git","args":[{"type":"word","value":"show"},{"type":"word","value":"origin/main:src/cli.rs"}],"fullText":"git show origin/main:src/cli.rs"},{"name":"head","args":[{"type":"number","value":"-80"}],"fullText":"head -80"},{"name":"echo","args":[{"type":"raw_string","value":"'---FILES---'"}],"fullText":"echo '---FILES---'"},{"name":"git","args":[{"type":"word","value":"show"},{"type":"word","value":"origin/main:tests/cli_e2e.rs"}],"fullText":"git show origin/main:tests/cli_e2e.rs"},{"name":"head","args":[{"type":"number","value":"-50"}],"fullText":"head -50"},{"name":"gh","args":[{"type":"word","value":"issue"},{"type":"word","value":"view"},{"type":"number","value":"17"},{"type":"word","value":"--json"},{"type":"word","value":"body"},{"type":"word","value":"--jq"},{"type":"word","value":".body"}],"fullText":"gh issue view 17 --json body --jq .body"}],"hasRedirects":true,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"allRedirectsAreDevNull":true,"redirects":[{"operator":">","destinationFds":[2],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/dev/null"},{"operator":">","destinationFds":[2],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/dev/null"},{"operator":">","destinationFds":[2],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/dev/null"}]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"Show origin/main cli files and issue 17 body JSON","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"42a2d878-df96-4e92-9fef-880dad80ff16","adminCommandDenylist":[],"requestId":"5d97dc51-aeb0-476e-a6af-a8d07968be1e"},"result":{"success":{"command":"cd /Users/user/work/delegate-fixtures && git fetch origin main 2>/dev/null; git show origin/main:src/cli.rs 2>/dev/null | head -80; echo '---FILES---'; git show origin/main:tests/cli_e2e.rs 2>/dev/null | head -50; gh issue view 17 --json body --jq .body","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"//! The `delegate` CLI: `run` starts a detached supervisor, `watch` reads job records.\n//! The record file under `$TMPDIR/delegate-jobs/` is the only link between them.\n\nuse crate::backends::cursor::make_cursor_adapter;\nuse crate::capability::map_capability;\nuse crate::git::capture_head;\nuse crate::index::build_deps;\nuse crate::job_registry::{JobRegistry, RegistryDeps, WaitOpts};\nuse crate::models::resolve_model;\nuse crate::prompt::status_block;\nuse crate::runner::build_argv;\nuse crate::status_record::{CliRecordWriter, cli_record_path};\nuse crate::types::{Capability, JobSpec, ResumeContext};\nuse crate::util::{random_uuid, resolve_path};\nuse std::io::{Read, Write};\nuse std::os::unix::fs::OpenOptionsExt;\nuse std::os::unix::process::CommandExt;\nuse std::process::{Command, Stdio};\nuse std::sync::Arc;\nuse std::time::{Duration, Instant};\n\nconst USAGE: &str = \"usage: delegate run --model M [--capability read-only|read-write] [--cwd D] [--prompt-file F]\\n       delegate watch <jobId>... [--timeout S]\";\n\n/// Bad input: reason on stderr, exit 2.\nstruct Usage(String);\n\nfn usage<T>(msg: impl Into<String>) -> Result<T, Usage> {\n    Err(Usage(msg.into()))\n}\n\npub fn main() -> i32 {\n    let args: Vec<String> = std::env::args().skip(1).collect();\n    let res = match args.first().map(String::as_str) {\n        Some(\"run\") => run(&args[1..]),\n        Some(\"watch\") => watch(&args[1..]),\n        Some(\"__supervise\") => return supervise(&args[1..]),\n        _ => usage(USAGE),\n    };\n    match res {\n        Ok(code) => code,\n        Err(Usage(m)) => {\n            eprintln!(\"{m}\");\n            2\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n/// Splits `--flag value` pairs from positionals.\nfn parse(args: &[String], flags: &[&str]) -> Result<(Vec<(String, String)>, Vec<String>), Usage> {\n    let (mut kv, mut pos) = (vec![], vec![]);\n    let mut it = args.iter();\n    while let Some(a) = it.next() {\n        if a.starts_with(\"--\") {\n            if !flags.contains(&a.as_str()) {\n                return usage(format!(\"unknown flag {a}\\n{USAGE}\"));\n            }\n            let Some(v) = it.next() else {\n                return usage(format!(\"{a} needs a value\"));\n            };\n            kv.push((a.clone(), v.clone()));\n        } else {\n            pos.push(a.clone());\n        }\n    }\n    Ok((kv, pos))\n}\n\nfn flag<'a>(kv: &'a [(String, String)], name: &str) -> Option<&'a str> {\n    kv.iter().find(|(k, _)| k == name).map(|(_, v)| v.as_str())\n}\n\nfn capability(name: &str) -> Result<(Capability, &'static str), Usage> {\n    match name {\n        \"read-only\" => Ok((Capability::Ask, \"read-only\")),\n        \"read-write\" => Ok((Capability::WriteUnsandboxed, \"read-write\")),\n        o => usage(format!(\n            \"unknown capability {o}: use read-only or read-write\"\n        )),\n    }\n}\n---FILES---\n//! Drives the real `delegate` binary as a process against a fake cursor-agent.\n\nuse serde_json::Value;\nuse std::io::Write;\nuse std::os::unix::fs::PermissionsExt;\nuse std::path::{Path, PathBuf};\nuse std::process::{Command, Output, Stdio};\nuse std::time::{Duration, Instant};\n\nconst FAKE_AGENT: &str = r#\"#!/bin/sh\nprintf '%s\\n' \"$@\" > \"$(dirname \"$0\")/argv.txt\"\nprintf '%s\\n' '{\"type\":\"tool_call\",\"subtype\":\"started\",\"tool_call\":{\"shellToolCall\":{\"args\":{\"command\":\"ls\"}}}}'\ncase \"$*\" in\n  *SLOW*) i=0; while [ ! -e \"$(dirname \"$0\")/go\" ] && [ $i -lt 200 ]; do sleep 0.05; i=$((i+1)); done ;;\nesac\ncase \"$*\" in\n  *ASKME*) printf '%s\\n' '{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"result\":\"Which db?\\nSTATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT\",\"session_id\":\"s-2\"}' ;;\n  *) printf '%s\\n' '{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"result\":\"391\\nSTATUS: DONE\",\"session_id\":\"s-1\"}' ;;\nesac\n\"#;\n\nstruct Env {\n    dir: PathBuf,\n}\n\nimpl Env {\n    fn new(name: &str) -> Self {\n        let dir = std::env::temp_dir().join(format!(\"cdm-cli-{name}-{}\", std::process::id()));\n        let _ = std::fs::remove_dir_all(&dir);\n        std::fs::create_dir_all(&dir).unwrap();\n        let agent = dir.join(\"agent.sh\");\n        std::fs::write(&agent, FAKE_AGENT).unwrap();\n        std::fs::set_permissions(&agent, std::fs::Permissions::from_mode(0o755)).unwrap();\n        Env { dir }\n    }\n\n    /// Lets SLOW jobs finish; until then they stay RUNNING (10s cap).\n    fn release(&self) {\n        std::fs::write(self.dir.join(\"go\"), \"\").unwrap();\n    }\n\n    fn argv(&self) -> Vec<String> {\n        let s = std::fs::read_to_string(self.dir.join(\"argv.txt\")).unwrap();\n        s.lines().map(String::from).collect()\n    }\n\n    fn delegate(&self, args: &[&str], stdin: Option<&str>) -> Output {\n        let mut child = Command::new(env!(\"CARGO_BIN_EXE_delegate\"))\n            .args(args)\n            .current_dir(&self.dir)\n## Parent\n\n#4\n\n## What to build\n\nClaude models run through `delegate`. `claude -p --output-format stream-json --verbose --model ...` with the user's full Claude Code configuration. read-only uses plan permission mode and read-write uses auto mode, or the fallback the probe findings on #4 chose. The session id is chosen before launch with `--session-id`, and resume uses `--resume`. Cost is the result line's `total_cost_usd`. Reuse the cursor parser where the streams match. Doctor checks the binary, version and login.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- # [ ] Parser tests on the recorded claude fixtures: answer, tool calls, resume, error, auto-mode refusal.\n- # [ ] run, resume, cancel and watch work end to end against a fake claude replaying fixtures.\n- # [ ] An opt-in live test does one real round trip and saves a fresh fixture.\n\n## Blocked by\n\n- #6 Record headless fixtures (recording script and probes)\n- #15 Backend split (prefactor)\n","stderr":"","executionTime":1698,"interleavedOutput":"//! The `delegate` CLI: `run` starts a detached supervisor, `watch` reads job records.\n//! The record file under `$TMPDIR/delegate-jobs/` is the only link between them.\n\nuse crate::backends::cursor::make_cursor_adapter;\nuse crate::capability::map_capability;\nuse crate::git::capture_head;\nuse crate::index::build_deps;\nuse crate::job_registry::{JobRegistry, RegistryDeps, WaitOpts};\nuse crate::models::resolve_model;\nuse crate::prompt::status_block;\nuse crate::runner::build_argv;\nuse crate::status_record::{CliRecordWriter, cli_record_path};\nuse crate::types::{Capability, JobSpec, ResumeContext};\nuse crate::util::{random_uuid, resolve_path};\nuse std::io::{Read, Write};\nuse std::os::unix::fs::OpenOptionsExt;\nuse std::os::unix::process::CommandExt;\nuse std::process::{Command, Stdio};\nuse std::sync::Arc;\nuse std::time::{Duration, Instant};\n\nconst USAGE: &str = \"usage: delegate run --model M [--capability read-only|read-write] [--cwd D] [--prompt-file F]\\n       delegate watch <jobId>... [--timeout S]\";\n\n/// Bad input: reason on stderr, exit 2.\nstruct Usage(String);\n\nfn usage<T>(msg: impl Into<String>) -> Result<T, Usage> {\n    Err(Usage(msg.into()))\n}\n\npub fn main() -> i32 {\n    let args: Vec<String> = std::env::args().skip(1).collect();\n    let res = match args.first().map(String::as_str) {\n        Some(\"run\") => run(&args[1..]),\n        Some(\"watch\") => watch(&args[1..]),\n        Some(\"__supervise\") => return supervise(&args[1..]),\n        _ => usage(USAGE),\n    };\n    match res {\n        Ok(code) => code,\n        Err(Usage(m)) => {\n            eprintln!(\"{m}\");\n            2\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n/// Splits `--flag value` pairs from positionals.\nfn parse(args: &[String], flags: &[&str]) -> Result<(Vec<(String, String)>, Vec<String>), Usage> {\n    let (mut kv, mut pos) = (vec![], vec![]);\n    let mut it = args.iter();\n    while let Some(a) = it.next() {\n        if a.starts_with(\"--\") {\n            if !flags.contains(&a.as_str()) {\n                return usage(format!(\"unknown flag {a}\\n{USAGE}\"));\n            }\n            let Some(v) = it.next() else {\n                return usage(format!(\"{a} needs a value\"));\n            };\n            kv.push((a.clone(), v.clone()));\n        } else {\n            pos.push(a.clone());\n        }\n    }\n    Ok((kv, pos))\n}\n\nfn flag<'a>(kv: &'a [(String, String)], name: &str) -> Option<&'a str> {\n    kv.iter().find(|(k, _)| k == name).map(|(_, v)| v.as_str())\n}\n\nfn capability(name: &str) -> Result<(Capability, &'static str), Usage> {\n    match name {\n        \"read-only\" => Ok((Capability::Ask, \"read-only\")),\n        \"read-write\" => Ok((Capability::WriteUnsandboxed, \"read-write\")),\n        o => usage(format!(\n            \"unknown capability {o}: use read-only or read-write\"\n        )),\n    }\n}\n---FILES---\n//! Drives the real `delegate` binary as a process against a fake cursor-agent.\n\nuse serde_json::Value;\nuse std::io::Write;\nuse std::os::unix::fs::PermissionsExt;\nuse std::path::{Path, PathBuf};\nuse std::process::{Command, Output, Stdio};\nuse std::time::{Duration, Instant};\n\nconst FAKE_AGENT: &str = r#\"#!/bin/sh\nprintf '%s\\n' \"$@\" > \"$(dirname \"$0\")/argv.txt\"\nprintf '%s\\n' '{\"type\":\"tool_call\",\"subtype\":\"started\",\"tool_call\":{\"shellToolCall\":{\"args\":{\"command\":\"ls\"}}}}'\ncase \"$*\" in\n  *SLOW*) i=0; while [ ! -e \"$(dirname \"$0\")/go\" ] && [ $i -lt 200 ]; do sleep 0.05; i=$((i+1)); done ;;\nesac\ncase \"$*\" in\n  *ASKME*) printf '%s\\n' '{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"result\":\"Which db?\\nSTATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT\",\"session_id\":\"s-2\"}' ;;\n  *) printf '%s\\n' '{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"result\":\"391\\nSTATUS: DONE\",\"session_id\":\"s-1\"}' ;;\nesac\n\"#;\n\nstruct Env {\n    dir: PathBuf,\n}\n\nimpl Env {\n    fn new(name: &str) -> Self {\n        let dir = std::env::temp_dir().join(format!(\"cdm-cli-{name}-{}\", std::process::id()));\n        let _ = std::fs::remove_dir_all(&dir);\n        std::fs::create_dir_all(&dir).unwrap();\n        let agent = dir.join(\"agent.sh\");\n        std::fs::write(&agent, FAKE_AGENT).unwrap();\n        std::fs::set_permissions(&agent, std::fs::Permissions::from_mode(0o755)).unwrap();\n        Env { dir }\n    }\n\n    /// Lets SLOW jobs finish; until then they stay RUNNING (10s cap).\n    fn release(&self) {\n        std::fs::write(self.dir.join(\"go\"), \"\").unwrap();\n    }\n\n    fn argv(&self) -> Vec<String> {\n        let s = std::fs::read_to_string(self.dir.join(\"argv.txt\")).unwrap();\n        s.lines().map(String::from).collect()\n    }\n\n    fn delegate(&self, args: &[&str], stdin: Option<&str>) -> Output {\n        let mut child = Command::new(env!(\"CARGO_BIN_EXE_delegate\"))\n            .args(args)\n            .current_dir(&self.dir)\n## Parent\n\n#4\n\n## What to build\n\nClaude models run through `delegate`. `claude -p --output-format stream-json --verbose --model ...` with the user's full Claude Code configuration. read-only uses plan permission mode and read-write uses auto mode, or the fallback the probe findings on #4 chose. The session id is chosen before launch with `--session-id`, and resume uses `--resume`. Cost is the result line's `total_cost_usd`. Reuse the cursor parser where the streams match. Doctor checks the binary, version and login.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- # [ ] Parser tests on the recorded claude fixtures: answer, tool calls, resume, error, auto-mode refusal.\n- # [ ] run, resume, cancel and watch work end to end against a fake claude replaying fixtures.\n- # [ ] An opt-in live test does one real round trip and saves a fresh fixture.\n\n## Blocked by\n\n- #6 Record headless fixtures (recording script and probes)\n- #15 Backend split (prefactor)\n","localExecutionTimeMs":1300},"isBackground":false},"description":"Show origin/main cli files and issue 17 body JSON"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"tool_911a93aa-63df-4227-a3c1-2702837340a","startedAtMs":"1790845581562","completedAtMs":"1790845583404"},"model_call_id":"5d97dc51-aeb0-476e-a6af-a8d07968be1e-1-poyw","session_id":"42a2d878-df96-4e92-9fef-880dad80ff16","timestamp_ms":1790845583380}
